{
  "coreName": "Supermodel",
  "systemId": "Model3",
  "systemNames": {
    "Model3": "Sega Model 3"
  },
  "author": "The Supermodel Team (trzy/supermodel: Bart Trzynadlowski, Nik Henson, Ian Curtis and others); chimera core by Sergio Martin",
  "url": "https://github.com/trzy/supermodel",
  "romFile": "game",
  "extensions": {
    ".zip": "Model3"
  },
  "_comment_extensions": "A Model 3 game is its ROM set: a zip named as Supermodel and MAME name it (vf3.zip, scud.zip, srally2.zip). Supermodel finds each of its files by its CRC32 through the game list the core carries (Supermodel's Games.xml), so the files' names inside do not matter.",
  "deterministic": true,
  "memoryLayoutMiB": [
    1024,
    16,
    16,
    16,
    3072
  ],
  "_memoryLayoutMiB_note": "sbrk, sealed, invisible, plain, mmap. Supermodel's one pool for the machine (about 250 MiB: RAM, the program ROM windows, the video, sound and MPEG ROMs), the Real3D's memories and the renderers' buffers, and Mesa's textures and buffers.",
  "video": {
    "_comment": "What Supermodel's New3D renderer and its 2D layers draw with OpenGL 4.1, on the Mesa llvmpipe compiled into the core (made to generate the same code on every computer): the Model 3's own 496x384.",
    "width": 496,
    "height": 384,
    "getBgra": "GetVideoBgra",
    "vsyncNumerator": 57524,
    "vsyncDenominator": 1000,
    "_comment_vsync": "The hardware's 57.524 frames a second."
  },
  "audio": {
    "_comment": "The sound board's two SCSP sound chips and the digital sound board's MPEG music, mixed to stereo as upstream mixes for two speakers: 766 or 767 samples a frame at 44100 Hz. samplesPerFrame is capacity.",
    "rate": 44100,
    "channels": 2,
    "samplesPerFrame": 981,
    "get": "GetAudio"
  },
  "lag": {
    "inputWasRead": "InputWasRead"
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "name": "startTime",
      "display": "setting.starttime",
      "type": "datetime",
      "default": 946684800,
      "description": "setting.starttime.about"
    },
    {
      "name": "idleSkip",
      "display": "setting.idleskip",
      "type": "bool",
      "default": true,
      "description": "setting.idleskip.about"
    }
  ],
  "firmware": [],
  "input": {
    "name": "Model 3 Cabinet",
    "_comment": "Every control at least one Model 3 cabinet has, by Supermodel's own inputs. A game shows only those its cabinet has (its <inputs> in Supermodel's game list); the others leave the input roll. Service and Test are the cabinet's service buttons. Gear 1 to 4 and Neutral set the 4-speed shifter; Shift Up and Down move it a gear, or work the up/down shifter. Trigger is a light gun's trigger (and an analog gun's left one); Off-screen points a light gun away from the screen, to reload.",
